n><span class=\"tag sub\">SUB</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/4417533/brief-encounter\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/4417533.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/4417533/brief-encounter\" target=\"\">Brief Encounter</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1945</span>                                        <span>87mins</span>                                        <span>UK</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Romance/Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by David Lean</span>                                        <span>Starring Celia Johnson, Trevor Howard, Stanley Holloway</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Returning home from a shopping trip to a nearby town, bored suburban housewife Laura Jesson (Celia Johnson) is thrown by happenstance into an acquaintance with virtuous doctor Alec Harvey (Trevor Howard). Their casual friendship soon develops during their weekly visits into something more emotionally fulfilling than either expected, and they must wrestle with the potential havoc their deepening relationship would have on their lives and the lives of those they love.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 12th July</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31626546\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/16630997/career-girls\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/pSgLXvL_El2nWq49iz9U6qJi-1YawS3Sx82BZaonXFM.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/16630997/career-girls\" target=\"\">Career Girls</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1997</span>                                        <span>87mins</span>                                        <span>France, UK</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Mike Leigh</span>                                        <span>Starring Katrin Cartlidge, Lynda Steadman, Kate Byers</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Annie (Lynda Steadman) is meeting up with her old college pal Hannah (Katrin Cartlidge) for the first time since they graduated six years ago. They bonded in school, despite their differences; now they&#39;ve become more mature and put their old problems behind them -- or so they think. Once they reunite, Annie realises that she hasn&#39;t fully overcome her past anxieties, while Hannah learns that she is still too insensitive to the feelings of others. Both women hope to make some changes.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMike Leigh cleverly weaves together past and present as we share their memories; the touching, the funny and the sometimes tragic.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 12th July</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31626536\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3487029/naked\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/3487029.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3487029/naked\" target=\"\">Naked</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1993</span>                                        <span>131mins</span>                                        <span>UK</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Comedy / Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Mike Leigh</span>                                        <span>Starring David Thewlis, Katrin Cartlidge, Lesley Sharp</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Johnny (David Thewlis) is a frenetic and destructive outsider who tears through the lives of others like an emotional tornado. On the run from Manchester, he seeks sanctuary with his ex-girlfriend Louise (Lesley Sharp) in London, where he immediately targets her vulnerable housemate Sophie (Katrin Cartlidge) with his unique blend of predatory charm. From there he embarks on a nocturnal odyssey across the city, dragging other disaffected souls into his orbit as he spirals towards his own personal apocalypse.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMike Leigh&rsquo;s Cannes-winning film is a masterful, controversial, and totally unforgettable exploration of society in free-fall at the tail end of Thatcher&rsquo;s Britain.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 12th July</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31626789\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:10 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617400/nirvanna-the-band-the-show-the-movie\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/lQ1kiMl_BImOHrYtGLLQIWGar6kcvf55mvSgnNJPTa0.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617400/nirvanna-the-band-the-show-the-movie\" target=\"\">Nirvanna the Band the Show the Movie</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2025</span>                                        <span>100mins</span>                                        <span>Canada</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Comedy / Fantasy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Matt Johnson</span>                                        <span>Starring Matt Johnson, Jay McCarrol, Ben Petrie</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>When their plan to book a show at the Rivoli goes horribly wrong, Matt and Jay accidentally travel back to the year 2008.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 12th July</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31626776\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 14th July</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31626770\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 15th July</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31626779\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 16th July</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31626763\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 18th July</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31626780\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n 